{"nbformat":4,"nbformat_minor":0,"metadata":{"colab":{"provenance":[],"authorship_tag":"ABX9TyOU7HSHupDAye0eUu6gx+3v"},"kernelspec":{"name":"python3","display_name":"Python 3"},"language_info":{"name":"python"}},"cells":[{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["**\"Debugging Olympics\" set of 10 slightly tough and unique Python debugging challenges**—ideal for students who've completed a Python course. Each question presents a buggy snippet with **intentional logical or subtle syntax issues**"],"metadata":{"id":"SOCq0PueIehR"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["---\n","\n","## 🧩 **Python Debugging Questions **\n","\n","---\n","\n","### ❓**1. Sum of Numbers**\n","\n","```python\n","def sum_numbers(n):\n","    total = 0\n","    for i in range(1, n):\n","        total += i\n","    return total\n","\n","print(sum_numbers(5))  # Expected: 15\n","```\n","\n","---\n","\n","### ❓**2. String Concatenation**\n","\n","```python\n","name = \"Alice\"\n","greeting = \"Hello, \" + name + \"!\" + 5\n","print(greeting)\n","```\n","\n","\n","---\n","\n","### ❓**3. Check Prime**\n","\n","```python\n","def is_prime(n):\n","    for i in range(2, n):\n","        if n % i == 0:\n","            return False\n","        else:\n","            return True\n","```\n","\n","\n","---\n","\n","### ❓**4. List Indexing**\n","\n","```python\n","fruits = [\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\"]\n","print(fruits[3])\n","```\n","\n","---\n","\n","### ❓**5. String Reversal**\n","\n","```python\n","def reverse_string(s):\n","    return s[::-1]\n","\n","print(reverse_string[\"hello\"])\n","```\n","\n","\n","---\n","\n","### ❓**6. Even or Odd**\n","\n","```python\n","num = 7\n","if num % 2 = 0:\n","    print(\"Even\")\n","else:\n","    print(\"Odd\")\n","```\n","\n","---\n","\n","### ❓**7. Append to List**\n","\n","```python\n","def add_item(item, my_list=[]):\n","    my_list.append(item)\n","    return my_list\n","\n","print(add_item(\"A\"))\n","print(add_item(\"B\"))\n","```\n","\n","\n","---\n","\n","### ❓**8. Dictionary Access**\n","\n","```python\n","person = {\"name\": \"Alice\", \"age\": 25}\n","print(person[\"gender\"])\n","```\n","\n","\n","---\n","\n","### ❓**9. For Loop Range**\n","\n","```python\n","for i in range(5):\n","    print(i + 1)\n","```\n","\n","---\n","\n","### ❓**10. Function Call Order**\n","\n","```python\n","def greet(name):\n","    return \"Hello \" + name\n","\n","print(greet)\n","```\n","\n","---\n","\n","## ✅ **Solutions Below**\n","\n","---\n","\n","### ✅ **1. Solution:**\n","\n","```python\n","for i in range(1, n + 1):  # Include n\n","```\n","\n","---\n","\n","### ✅ **2. Solution:**\n","\n","```python\n","greeting = \"Hello, \" + name + \"!\" + str(5)\n","```\n","\n","---\n","\n","### ✅ **3. Solution:**\n","\n","```python\n","for i in range(2, n):\n","    if n % i == 0:\n","        return False\n","return True\n","```\n","\n","---\n","\n","### ✅ **4. Solution:**\n","\n","```python\n","print(fruits[2])  # Index 2 is 'cherry'\n","```\n","\n","---\n","\n","### ✅ **5. Solution:**\n","\n","```python\n","print(reverse_string(\"hello\"))  # Use parentheses, not brackets\n","```\n","\n","---\n","\n","### ✅ **6. Solution:**\n","\n","```python\n","if num % 2 == 0:\n","```\n","\n","---\n","\n","### ✅ **7. Solution:**\n","\n","```python\n","def add_item(item, my_list=None):\n","    if my_list is None:\n","        my_list = []\n","    my_list.append(item)\n","    return my_list\n","```\n","\n","---\n","\n","### ✅ **8. Solution:**\n","\n","```python\n","print(person.get(\"gender\", \"Not specified\"))\n","```\n","\n","---\n","\n","### ✅ **9. Solution:**\n","\n","```python\n","for i in range(1, 6):\n","    print(i)\n","```\n","\n","*(If the goal is to print from 1 to 5)*\n","\n","---\n","\n","### ✅ **10. Solution:**\n","\n","```python\n","print(greet(\"Alice\"))\n","```\n"],"metadata":{"id":"U5s582OwJptF"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":[],"metadata":{"id":"TPS9waovJhZB"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["# Advanced"],"me